From 6947eddbceeb3378eda75e653571fbd5f0c7a610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UML Android bring-up <uml@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:39:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/12] um: add a thunk BPF "JIT"

Android's BPF loaders need a kernel with a BPF JIT: netd writes
bpf_jit_enable, and the verifier only accepts programs with callbacks or
bpf-to-bpf calls when they can be JITed. UML has no JIT, so emit, for every
program, a short native stub that jumps into the interpreter entry taking
the instruction array as its sixth argument. The stubs are placed in a page
arena inside the kernel image, within the 32-bit reach of __bpf_call_base,
and the arena is made executable through the host.

x86_64 and arm64 host encodings are provided.
